{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner dispositions for the complete 232-line one-file owner proposal, freshly read at /tmp/artroom-file-version-design/notes/2026-10-08-i5-edit-selective-assembly.md, SHA256 c31e37a30f6483e9065a1199ed75a0cf5da2ff905d270e3301508f4df2e47f11. Existing configuration/outcome bodies and actual checker/lane/version interfaces were read. These are concrete selections for the same proposal's reviewable successor, not approval to implement unsupported wire changes or activate them.\n\nReserve artroom-check-configuration-2 for exactly the proposed six existing configuration fields plus checkout:{kind:\"one-file\",abi:Digest}. Keep artroom-check-configuration-1, its digest framing and six-field integration meaning unchanged. The configuration selector is the closed union of those two literals and their Digest. The ABI digest is the raw artifact identity of a complete canonical owner-reviewed record with format artroom-one-file-check-abi-1; it must bind actual target input, authorized base read, tree/index/worktree/HEAD checkout, report/details and immutable image compatibility contracts, not a name-only assertion.\n\nCombine rules/destination changes with the already selected unshipped c4 native @3 cohort, rather than preparing two different meanings at @3. Reserve platform:rules@3 and platform:destination@3 for that single combined reviewed meaning; the owner must verify all pending/shipped allocation evidence before freezing it. Changed register/directory child-creation or eligibility semantics require their own fresh unused coherent identities; freeze the actual complete birth/observation/runtime tuple and do not assume that a root count or unchanged family name proves compatibility. Preserve every shipped @1/@2 byte and actual historical bundle. Amended change/full-demo definitions receive their own new content digests; old pinned lane definitions are not rewritten or repinned. The existing checker integration contract remains selectable on its actual old configuration/ABI; the new one-file format has a distinct schema identity and explicit dispatch.\n\nSelect a closed one-file runner report with format artroom-one-file-check-run-1, exact job FactRef, complete configuration selector, ABI Digest and target identity, plus the existing started/image/environment/steps/end fields. Target identity is exactly kind:\"one-file\", manifest FactRef, base, tree, path, digest and size; content is an input bound by that manifest/digest/size and is not duplicated into the report or details. Replace boolean checkout in this new format with either {confirmed:false,reason} or {confirmed:true,head,indexTree,worktreeTree}; the confirmed hashes must equal actual base/candidate as appropriate, and the service compares every job/selector/ABI/target member against its independently read job before judging. A scalar checkout=true or compatible label cannot pass. Reasons are closed, bounded codes from the declared reader/checkout contract, never arbitrary exception/output text. Keep the old integration RunReport parser unchanged.\n\nSelect Details with format artroom-one-file-check-details-1 and exactly provenance. Its provenance retains exact job, complete selector, ABI and target identity; declared/resolved image, environment digest, validated checkout classification, configured step names/statuses and the service's run record. It contains no content, bearer, raw output or arbitrary exception message. Details use the existing raw canonical-byte digest framing: these format strings are schema identities, not invented hash domains. The new validator and signed result must bind that digest to this job/tree/selector and actual checked target. Current integration Details/RunProvenance bytes keep their meaning. Preserve existing passed/failed/check-error distinction and error precedence; add only explicitly specified new target/ABI incompatibility or mismatch codes to this successor, with unknown/malformed/nonconfirmed cases non-pass and